 america  and then we flew over and i it was just  very exciting  no sarah why does it look like you're in  batman's plane and the one to your left  is like a delta flight on its way  totally you're totally right  yeah what's that about yeah so the  aircraft on our left is the b-52  and uh that is our workhorse bomber uh  she's been around for a long time  uh she's our she's a reliable bomber  there but uh yeah we've got the stealth  and the lead yeah  there you go drop the mic that's you do  you have any advice  you know right now uh for i don't know  any woman who like maybe stressing out  there in the world  yeah absolutely so everybody gets  stressed right but uh  it's kind of two-fold how i manage my  stress my sister is actually a  neuropsychologist  so she has really hammered home the  importance of mindfulness  in the day-to-day uh so i try to  practice that as much as i can  and remind myself it's important but but  really in the execution phase  i maintain my calm just because of all  the extensive training we do  so whether it's in the simulator or  flying or studying  or mission prepping and briefing we uh  we are constantly training so when i  step to that aircraft and take off i  really fall back on all the training  that i have  uh because you know we got to make  decisions on the fly and uh  we're going very fast decisions need to  come in uh  very fast so i just really fall back on  that training could i ever come get in  the simulator  sometime to see what's like yeah  absolutely come out to whiteman we'll be  uh i will personally give you guys a  tour of the jet in the simulator  okay thank you oh my god  can i can i i want to come yeah yeah you  could come okay  and i'll like there's a little bit of  security prep that we'll have to do  beforehand but  am i correct in this um sarah that you  when you were little you went to super  bowls and  saw the planes fly over uh close yeah so  my parents  i grew up in cleveland and they took us  to the cleveland air show pretty much  every year  so i got to see not only the static  aircraft there but but all the aircraft  fly  and that's kind of where my passion  kicked in just seeing the aircraft  hearing them feeling it um and then when  i was 11 my sister  was marching in the rose bowl parade so  my parents took us out there so  yeah right right when uh right when the  parade starts the b2 does its flyover  and i had never  seen anything like that in my life and i  just thought it was  the coolest thing as a kid and it really  stuck with me  for the rest of my life what do you say  to little girls  um who may have the same dream that you  did and wanted to fly a plane  one day so any little girl or a little  boy out there that  that wants to fly think aviation is cool  maybe has a passion for it to just go  chase your dreams you know we live in  this great country where we're afforded  the opportunity to go  chase our dreams so go check it out get  into the world of aviation see if you  like it  and you know most importantly don't let  anybody out there convince you that you  can't do it  you are living proof of that thank you  captain sarah kosciuba i am just  so honored to meet you me too it's very  exciting  [Applause]  [Music]
 

